course: dictionary
lesson: 14746
title: Formal words in law and church
level: primary-6
stars: 0
explain: Promulgation is a long, formal word, so look for its clues. It comes from promulgate, a verb meaning to announce something publicly. «The promulgation of the new law took place in the town square, where the mayor read it aloud to everyone.» The clues are law, read aloud and everyone, so promulgation must be the official public announcement of the law.
explain: Use the swap test. Put a simpler word into the sentence in place of the hard word and see if it still makes sense. «The announcement of the new law took place in the town square» still works, so announcement is a good match. Promulgation is a more formal way of saying it.
explain: The word also has other meanings. Spreading an idea or belief widely among people can be called promulgation, as can the official announcement of a teaching by a church. In every case, the clues show that something is being made known widely and officially.
fact: Promulgation is a noun, and it is usually uncountable.
fact: «Promulgation» means the official public announcement of a new law or rule, so that it comes into force.
fact: «Promulgation» can also mean spreading an idea or belief widely among people.
fact: In church, «promulgation» means the official announcement of a teaching.
fact: Clue words for promulgation include law, rule, decree, official and announce.
exercise: «The king ordered the promulgation of the new law.» What is promulgation here? | A tax paid by farmers | A long wait for a reply | A secret meeting of the king's advisers | * The official public announcement of the law
exercise: «The promulgation of the rule was read out in every school.» Find and copy the clue that tells you it was announced. | * read out | rule | school | every
exercise: «Her teacher spoke about the promulgation of a new idea across the country.» Which meaning fits best? | Hiding an idea from everyone | * Spreading an idea or belief widely among people | Drawing a picture of a flag | Forgetting a belief
test: What is the promulgation of a law? | A painting of a judge | A list of school rules to copy out | A broken promise made in private | * The official public announcement that makes it start
test: In church, what is a promulgation? | A song sung at weddings | * The official announcement of a church teaching | A quiet prayer said alone | A kind of church bell
exam: Which word could replace promulgation in «The promulgation of the decree was made on the radio»? | silence | mistake | ruin | * announcement
